course: dictionary
lesson: 5517
title: Leaky
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so look at the words around them to find the right one. «Priya built a model of her own house, including the leaky tap.» A tap is something water flows through, so leaky here must describe a tap that lets water escape.
explain: Leaky means having a hole or crack that lets liquid or gas escape, or get in. A leaky tap drips, a leaky boot lets water in, and a leaky tent gets everyone wet. «Think of a leaky old house: no single drip brings it down, but many leaks together, year after year, do.»
explain: Informal speech has a second meaning. A person or group that lets secrets out can also be called leaky. A «leaky» government lets secrets reach the newspapers. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Leaky is an adjective, and it changes to leakier and leakiest.
fact: «Leaky» means having a hole or crack that lets liquid or gas escape or get in.
fact: «A leaky tap» drips, «a leaky roof» lets rain in, and «a leaky boat» lets water in.
fact: In informal speech, a leaky person or group lets secrets out.
fact: In science problems, a leaky tank or bucket loses water over time.
exercise: «Priya built a model of her own house, including the leaky tap.» What does leaky mean here? | Made of brown blocks | Very shiny and clean | Hot to touch | *Has a hole that lets water escape
exercise: A «leaky» government lets secrets reach the press. What does leaky mean here? | Makes very loud noises | Keeps all its secrets safe | Is full of water | *Lets secrets out
exercise: Which one is a leaky boot? | *A boot that lets water in | A boot that keeps every drop out | A boot that is much too big | A boot with gold buckles
test: Which word is the comparative form of leaky? | leakyer | *leakier | leaker | leakiest
test: The tent was leaky, so what most likely happened? | Everyone stayed perfectly dry | The tent floated away | *Everyone got wet | Nobody noticed a thing
exam: Read: «Think of a leaky old house: no single drip brings it down.» What does leaky suggest about the house? | It is brand new and perfect | It has no roof at all | *It has holes or cracks that let water in | It is made of gold
